== Phase 1: Vendor history selection and assessment validation (pure helpers) ==
Provider: codex
Model: gpt-5.4
Status: starting Codex phase run.
Phase 1 is implemented and scoped to the pure-helper surface.

I added the `flag-payment-request` policy entry at authority level 3 and bumped the policy version to `v3`. I also added `lib/roles/riskAssess.js` with only the Phase 1 helpers: vendor ID normalization, deterministic vendor-history selection, fenced-JSON parsing, and strict assessment normalization/validation. The stale `v2` assertion in `test/phase5.test.js` was updated, and focused Phase 1 coverage was added in `test/riskAssess.test.js`.

Verification:
- `node --check lib/roles/riskAssess.js` passed.
- `node --test test/riskAssess.test.js test/phase5.test.js` passed.
- The runner command with the documented skip pattern passed:
  `npm install && node --check bin/e3d-corp && node --test --test-skip-pattern='real knowledge-base results|records evidence for the repo lookup|real integration returns real repos' $(find test -name '*.test.js' ! -name 'e3dTradeAcceptance.test.js')`

Issue:
- `npm run check` still fails in this workspace for pre-existing non-Phase-1 reasons: `test/e3dTradeAcceptance.test.js` imports a missing external `e3d-trade` module, and the real-integration tests in `test/phase3.test.js` and `test/phase8.test.js` expect live knowledge-base results. I recorded that in the required handoff at [.codex-spec-runner/summaries/phase-1.md](/var/folders/vn/jrwn6x0579v_26grcpvwp_200000gn/T/e3d-pilot.impl-5802bc1f2fe4-repo-20260918102643.dhBOID/.codex-spec-runner/summaries/phase-1.md).
