== Phase 2: Risk assessment orchestration (runRiskAssess) ==
Provider: codex
Model: gpt-5.4
Status: starting Codex phase run.
**Phase 2 Status**

Implemented `runRiskAssess` in [lib/roles/riskAssess.js](/var/folders/vn/jrwn6x0579v_26grcpvwp_200000gn/T/e3d-pilot.impl-5802bc1f2fe4-repo-20260918102643.dhBOID/lib/roles/riskAssess.js) and expanded [test/riskAssess.test.js](/var/folders/vn/jrwn6x0579v_26grcpvwp_200000gn/T/e3d-pilot.impl-5802bc1f2fe4-repo-20260918102643.dhBOID/test/riskAssess.test.js) for the end-to-end request-to-proposal path. The role now resolves a single configured provider, loads bounded vendor-relevant history, builds the assessment prompt, validates grounded evidence IDs, and creates exactly one pending `flag-payment-request` proposal without appending decisions, actions, or provider telemetry. I also wrote the handoff to [.codex-spec-runner/summaries/phase-2.md](/var/folders/vn/jrwn6x0579v_26grcpvwp_200000gn/T/e3d-pilot.impl-5802bc1f2fe4-repo-20260918102643.dhBOID/.codex-spec-runner/summaries/phase-2.md).

**Verification**

Passed:
- `npm install`
- `node --check bin/e3d-corp`
- `node --test --test-skip-pattern='real knowledge-base results|records evidence for the repo lookup|real integration returns real repos' $(find test -name '*.test.js' ! -name 'e3dTradeAcceptance.test.js')`

Issue still present outside this phase:
- Bare `npm run check` fails for pre-existing reasons unrelated to `runRiskAssess`: `test/e3dTradeAcceptance.test.js` imports a missing external `e3d-trade` module, and the real knowledge-base integration tests in `test/phase3.test.js` and `test/phase8.test.js` currently return `unavailable`.
